        "original_id": "e17e9514-e2f1-5970-bb8b-fb4034a1a132",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Del Davis\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Works: \"A World Without Love\", \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop music duo Peter and Gordon.\n- \"A World Without Love\" was the biggest hit of Peter and Gordon and was a No. 1 million-selling song.\n- \"A World Without Love\" was written by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
